{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"agent_message","text":"The reference keeps both normalization tensors in channel-major, noncontiguous layout, so each following linear projection must handle a strided last dimension. I’m prototyping a fused centered-variance Triton normalization that uses the reference formula and writes contiguous output. The key test is end-to-end rounding—not just normalized-value error—because attention can amplify one-bit changes."}}
