{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"agent_message","text":"The fused normalization matches 99.994% of normalized bfloat16 values, but the first norm feeds an argmax-sensitive attention stage, so those few one-bit differences spread globally. I’m retaining the exact first norm and testing fusion only for the second norm, where errors flow through smooth FFN operations and should remain localized enough for tolerance."}}
